Today I ascended for the second time in 3.1.3, as a Wizard, and doubled
my previous score (as a Priestess) to 4.4 million.  (Having 10
dilithium crystals and 100 or so other gems didn't hurt).  Here are
some observations from my quests:

- You DON'T need to have the silver bell, Book of the Dead, or
candelabrum after you reach Moloch's Sanctum.  All you need to ascend
is the Amulet of Yendor.  Don't waste inventory weight and space
carrying them around once you have used them for the ritual.

- (This one courtesy of my roommate, an inveterate hacker) Make sure to
put your bags of holding into an ordinary sack, as the Book, Amulet,
Wizard, and other nasties will curse your stuff, and a cursed loaded
bag of holding will really weigh you down!  (I used six bags of holding
in my latest game, all blessed of course, and if any of them had gotten
cursed I would have been in serious trouble).

- I was warned by my roommate that genociding large number of monsters
would result in even nastier monsters being created in Gehennom.  From
my experience, this is NOT true. I genocided 37 species (LDnHVcg -
maybe more, I don't remember) and the results were really amusing: Vlad
was the ONLY monster in the top level of his tower; when the Wizard
summoned monsters only a couple of quadrapeds and other not-so-nasties
(by that level anyway) showed up; etc.

- Sting may be underrated as a weapon; I made it all the way down to
the castle level with just that (well, I did enchant it to +4
eventually).  My god refused to give my any magic weapons despite
literally hundreds of sacrifices; I later discovered that this was
partly due to my roommate's cockatriced statue down near the castle
level already having three of them (Excalibur, Magicbane, and
Firebrand.  By the end of the game I also had Sunsword, but the only
weapon I really used from then on was my +7 Excalibur.)  I was also
unable to get any named weapons out of the wand of wishing; my roommate
claims I should have blessed it first, but I still think it should have
given my Vorpal Blade at the very least after many wasted attempts.

- I didn't max out all of my stats this time (I did when I was a
Priestess) - my charisma was only 10 at the end (I know, Big Deal).  I
also only made it to level 23 - not enough wraiths, and I didn't bother
cursing the bell to get more.  And my ingrateful god gave me NO
intrinsics, NO weapons, and did NOT make me the Envoy of Balance
despite the aforementioned hundreds of sacrifices.  The only thing he
ever granted was a spellbook that I already had (magic missile).  But I
managed to win anyway, so don't despair if things aren't going your way
- they may improve drastically (I started with a strength of 8 and
little useful in my inventory except a wand of polymorph, and was
unable to find a bag of any kind until rather far into the game).

- Wands of teleportation seem not to work in Gehennom once you have the
Amulet, but scrolls still do. Just trying to use the wands still uses a
charge.

I'm sure most of you hack addicts have gotten better scores and already
know all of this stuff, but just a year ago I had never even heard of
this game so I know that there is always more to discover... Happy
Hacking!

